<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to offer 2-yr bonds of HUF 20bln on Feb 27.</title>
<headline>Hungary to offer 2-yr bonds of HUF 20bln on Feb 27.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 20 billion forint worth of the two-year government bonds of 1999/F series on February 27, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    3 March 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		   12 April 1999</p>
<p>    Bills on offer		     20,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price			96.96 pct</p>
<p>Average yield of two-year</p>
<p>	bonds at last auction (Jan 30)   18.58 pct @</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.5 percent, payable semi-anually starting from October 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
